# Oracle probe (L11.9, ADR 0186) — negative indexing is one rule (i < 0 => i + len)
# shared by read, write and slice. Today xs[-1] traps on both backends and a literal
# [1,2,3][-1] takes the compiler down (L11.4, and the L11.8 no-panic contract).
xs = [1, 2, 3]
print(xs[-1])
print(xs[-2])
ys = [1, 2, 3]
print(ys[-1])
